  "notes": "Their excuse «إنما كنا نخوض ونلعب» (65:4-7) is not glossed; As-Sa'di's «مبينا عدم عذرهم وكذبهم» follows. Their mockery is not quoted (As-Sa'di's report of it is not used). A book for «سورة», light for «إن نعف عن طائفة». STAGING v4: c1 (64): a town by day; three men (the hypocrites) lower their heads in fear on 64:1 (both tafsirs: they fear a surah exposing what they hide; no head-lowering under the geometric plate); a book plate on 64:6 (the surah) and a geometric plate from 64:13 (Allah will bring out what they fear). Their mockery is not acted (64:12 is an ironic command; nothing is shown as obeying it), and no plate starts on 64:11. c2 (65-66) stays ambient under a night sky (no central light source) with the background quiet over both verses (Allah addresses the Prophet, the command to say, and His own first-person speech in 66:7-13): their excuse is given to the Prophet (As-Sa'di: they came to him apologising), so it cannot be acted without an addressee; the pardon plate of 66:7 is now geometric instead of light (a light plate must not start next to His act of pardoning). The cover moves to the ambient chapter (66:8, the geometric plate on the night sky), matching the title about revering the religion."
